   "[rule[r1]] dependsOn[1].targetRef \"Section 6.01(b)(28)\" is not a rule in this compilation unit - preserved as an unresolved cross-unit dependency (review required), never guessed or dropped",
   "This shard compiles Section 6.01(b) exceptions (4) through (11) and (20) only; clauses (12) through (19) (and various lettered sub-clauses thereof) fall in a source region explicitly owned by other shards and were not compiled here, per the gap notice in the operative text.",
   "Section 6.01(b)(4)(a)'s aggregate cap is a self-contained three-part formula (greater-of fixed/EBITDA-percentage amount, plus First Lien Leverage Ratio headroom, plus Effective-Date outstanding Capitalized Lease Obligations); it is also stated to aggregate with Refinancing Indebtedness incurred under Section 6.01(b)(13) to refinance (4)-basket debt - that cross-section sharing is preserved via a dependsOn (SHARES_CAPACITY_WITH) rather than restated as an independent cap, consistent with getReferencedProvision confirmation that Section 6.01(b)(13) is indeed the operative 'Refinancing Indebtedness' basket referencing back to Section 6.01(b)(4).",
   "Unsecured Capitalized Leases are expressly carved out of the (4)(a) cap and instead permitted in unlimited amount under Section 6.01(b)(28) (text of that section obtained and quoted); represented as a dependsOn, not as part of the ADD formula.",
   "Clauses (5) through (11) and (20) each state no dollar ceiling, so they are represented with UNLIMITED_CAPACITY (gatedBy null) plus their respective qualitative conditions/exceptions (e.g., 30-day LC reimbursement cure, ordinary-course/consistent-with-past-practice requirements, subordination-on-trigger provisions, speculative-hedging exclusion) rather than a fabricated dollar amount.",
   "Several sibling inventory items in clauses (7)-(9) describe 'deemed incurrence/issuance' anti-abuse triggers (loss of exemption upon certain transfers or status changes); these are represented as non-gating-formula conditions on the relevant permission rules since the IR has no dedicated 'deeming' primitive, but their substance (trigger + carve-outs + consequence of non-permission) is preserved in the condition description and citations.",
   "Terms such as 'Disqualified Stock', 'Consolidated EBITDA', 'Consolidated First Lien Debt', 'Purchase Money Obligations', and 'Sale and Lease-Back Transactions' are referenced only by name (METRIC_REFERENCE/DEFINED_TERM_REFERENCE or plain text) without expanding their own definitions, consistent with several of these being flagged out-of-scope/budget-exhausted in the supplied context and not being required to state this provision's own economics.",
   "Low-severity UNRESOLVED_DEFINED_TERM and AMBIGUOUS_RELATIVE_REFERENCE flags noted in the task context did not surface any specific ambiguity within the clauses actually compiled here beyond what is already reflected in the dependsOn entries."
